></mover></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn></math> millimeters. Since the ratio of the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper B\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math> to the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction x Over 136 EndFraction equals three fourths\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>136</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals StartFraction 3 left parenthesis 136 right parenthesis Over 4 EndFraction\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>136</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 102\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>102</mn></math>. Therefore, the length of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper B\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"102\"><mn>102</mn></math> millimeters.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the scale factor by which the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math> ratio is multiplied that results in the side lengths of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"triangle upper A upper B upper C\"><mo>△</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math>, not the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper B\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math>, not the length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper B\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover></math>.</p>","externalid":"aa7ee350-2124-4fd5-afe1-f10a1f785d05","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1755117017722,"updateDate":1755117017722}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017722, 1755117017722),
