></mrow></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext=\"792 equals left parenthesis 36 right parenthesis left parenthesis upper S upper T right parenthesis\"><mn>792</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>36</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"22 equals upper S upper T\"><mn>22</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math>. Therefore, the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math>. It's also given that point <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi>\n</math> lies on <math alttext=\"line segment upper R upper S\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, point <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math> lies on&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper L upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper R upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>. It follows that angle <math alttext=\"upper L upper K upper S\"><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is a right angle. Since triangles <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"upper L upper S upper K\"><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></math> share angle <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math> and have right angles <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math>, respectively, triangles <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper L upper S upper K\"><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></math> are similar triangles. Therefore, the ratio of the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper R upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> to the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper L upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is equal to the ratio of the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> to the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>. If the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper R upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math> and the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper L upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math>, it follows that the ratio of the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper R upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> to the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper L upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 72 Over 24 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>72</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>, so the ratio of the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> to the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"StartFraction 22 Over upper S upper K EndFraction equals 3\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper S upper K\"><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"22 equals left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis left parenthesis upper S upper K right parenthesis\"><mn>22</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 22 Over 3 EndFraction equals upper S upper K\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></math>. Since the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, <math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math>, is the sum of the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper S upper K\"><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, <math alttext=\"StartFraction 22 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>22</mn>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>, and the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper K upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>, it follows that the length of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"line segment upper K upper T\"><mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"22 minus StartFraction 22 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"StartFraction 44 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>44</mn>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. Note that 44/3, 14.66, and 14.67 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","externalid":"21c2c201-137b-4fd3-9fa4-520c318b5319","correct_answer":["14.66","14.67","44/3"]},"createDate":1691007959838,"updateDate":1691007959838}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959838, 1691007959838),
