w.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48 t c m squared\"><mn>48</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The four lateral faces include two with dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"eight thirds c m\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15 cm\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>&nbsp;and two with dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 t c m\"><mn>9</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15 c m\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The total area of these four lateral faces is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis eight thirds right parenthesis left parenthesis 15 right parenthesis plus 2 left parenthesis 9 t right parenthesis left parenthesis 15 right parenthesis c m squared\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"80 plus 270 t c m squared\"><mn>80</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>270</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Adding this to the total area of the two bases yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48 t plus 270 t plus 80\"><mn>48</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>270</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"318 t plus 80 c m squared\"><mn>318</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the expression, which represents the surface area, in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the right rectangular prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"318 t plus 80\"><mn>318</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the volume, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m cubed\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, not the surface area, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"62ec6574","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"70b95bcc-29ac-4b72-909d-c64fad3c9c1d","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"635e6fcf-2309-4ae9-8146-cb14f14c977d","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right rectangular prism has a base area of <math alttext=\"24 t square centimeters left parenthesis c m squared right parenthesis\"><mn>24</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math>. The length of the base of the rectangular prism is <math alttext=\"eight thirds c m\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, and the height of the rectangular prism is <math alttext=\"15 c m\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Which expression represents the surface area, in <math alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the right rectangular prism?</p>","keys":["4cd53c50-49b4-409c-b7fd-0042308a357f"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"e19647cf-6f98-4e69-923a-10557cd33f1a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"48 t plus 160\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>48</mn>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>160</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4cd53c50-49b4-409c-b7fd-0042308a357f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"318 t plus 80\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>318</mn>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>80</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"47d54639-6386-495c-89ca-1f39ead8ff3e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,968 t plus 80\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>1,968</mn>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>80</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9ebaf904-77b0-470e-adb1-79f03f209c11","content":"<p><math alttext=\"360 t\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>360</mn>\n\t<mi>t</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It's given that the base area of the right rectangular prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24 t c m squared\"><mn>24</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and the length of the base is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"eight thirds c m\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Dividing the base area by the length yields the width: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 24 t Over eight thirds EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 24 t right parenthesis left parenthesis three eighths right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 t c m\"><mn>9</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. It's also given that the height of the prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15 cm\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. A right rectangular prism has two rectangular bases and four rectangular lateral faces. The total area of the two bases is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis 24 t right parenthesis\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48 t c m squared\"><mn>48</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The four lateral faces include two with dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"eight thirds c m\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15 cm\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>&nbsp;and two with dimensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 t c m\"><mn>9</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15 c m\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The total area of these four lateral faces is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis eight thirds right parenthesis left parenthesis 15 right parenthesis plus 2 left parenthesis 9 t right parenthesis left parenthesis 15 right parenthesis c m squared\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"80 plus 270 t c m squared\"><mn>80</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>270</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Adding this to the total area of the two bases yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"48 t plus 270 t plus 80\"><mn>48</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>270</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"318 t plus 80 c m squared\"><mn>318</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Thus, the expression, which represents the surface area, in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the right rectangular prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"318 t plus 80\"><mn>318</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>80</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the volume, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m cubed\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, not the surface area, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m squared\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>","externalid":"70b95bcc-29ac-4b72-909d-c64fad3c9c1d","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1776362727992,"updateDate":1776362727992}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727992, 1776362727992),
