<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the figure, two lines intersect at a point. If <math alttext="w equals 136"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>136</mn></math>, what is the value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4cfb058c-4401-4abd-b0fd-2690e8199c07","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7eddd33e-534e-4171-b501-dace2f6e70b8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"34827234-aaa0-489d-a74b-5999fcced2b4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"68\"><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"492edbc9-b612-49b6-8ab2-5a4891856bd5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["492edbc9-b612-49b6-8ab2-5a4891856bd5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. In the figure shown, the angles with measures <math alttext="w degree"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext="z degree"><mi>z</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, <math alttext="w equals z"><mrow>
	<mi>w</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>z</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, if <math alttext="w equals 136"><mrow>
	<mi>w</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>136</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the value of <math alttext="z"><mi>z</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="136"><mn>136</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of an angle that's supplementary, not congruent, to the angle with measure <math alttext="w degree"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>
