4a1.1,1.1,0,0,1-.339-.805,1.042,1.042,0,0,1,.339-.785,1.133,1.133,0,0,1,.805-.319,1.091,1.091,0,0,1,1.1,1.1,1.131,1.131,0,0,1-.32.805,1.036,1.036,0,0,1-.784.339A1.1,1.1,0,0,1,245.533,193.184Z\"></path></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 2 intersecting lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>At the intersection of the 2 lines, the angles are labeled clockwise from top as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Top: w°</li>\n<li>Right: unlabeled</li>\n<li>Bottom: z°</li>\n<li>Left: unlabeled</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, two lines intersect at a point. If <math alttext=\"w equals 136\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>136</mn></math>, what is the value of <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4cfb058c-4401-4abd-b0fd-2690e8199c07","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7eddd33e-534e-4171-b501-dace2f6e70b8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"34827234-aaa0-489d-a74b-5999fcced2b4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"68\"><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"492edbc9-b612-49b6-8ab2-5a4891856bd5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["492edbc9-b612-49b6-8ab2-5a4891856bd5"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. In the figure shown, the angles with measures <math alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"z degree\"><mi>z</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, <math alttext=\"w equals z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, if <math alttext=\"w equals 136\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>136</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of an angle that's supplementary, not congruent, to the angle with measure <math alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357408,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"64d1f49f","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1730147357408,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"c6b681f6-504a-4e3a-8c73-a1cc8632d86b","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"c47f9914-475f-4079-8cfd-53f90ba08715","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"4cfb058c-4401-4abd-b0fd-2690e8199c07"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"7eddd33e-534e-4171-b501-dace2f6e70b8"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"68\"><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"34827234-aaa0-489d-a74b-5999fcced2b4"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"492edbc9-b612-49b6-8ab2-5a4891856bd5"}],"externalid":"c6b681f6-504a-4e3a-8c73-a1cc8632d86b","keys":["492edbc9-b612-49b6-8ab2-5a4891856bd5"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. In the figure shown, the angles with measures <math alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"z degree\"><mi>z</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, <math alttext=\"w equals z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, if <math alttext=\"w equals 136\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>136</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the value of <math alttext=\"z\"><mi>z</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"136\"><mn>136</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of an angle that's supplementary, not congruent, to the angle with measure <math alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"247.442\" height=\"197.652\" viewBox=\"0 0 247.442 197.652\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A diagram of 2 intersecting lines. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"fe0ea055-8ee1-4e3a-9bc4-1bd766077a9e\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><line x1=\"24.354\" y1=\"0.945\" x2=\"224.446\" y2=\"133.332\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><line x1=\"229.786\" y1=\"9.828\" x2=\"19.013\" y2=\"124.449\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><path d=\"M120.681,47.71a.543.543,0,0,1,.484.281,1.366,1.366,0,0,1,.175.727,5.82,5.82,0,0,1-.116,1.027l-.582,2.965a9.579,9.579,0,0,0-.156,1.221,1.326,1.326,0,0,0,.175.776.732.732,0,0,0,.62.232,1.635,1.635,0,0,0,1-.5,6.632,6.632,0,0,0,1.095-1.279q.467-3.818.64-4.477c.168-.645.426-.969.775-.969q.736,0,.736.911a10.714,10.714,0,0,1-.794,3.43,12.228,12.228,0,0,0-.135,1.241,3.454,3.454,0,0,0,.164,1.289.627.627,0,0,0,.63.358,1.933,1.933,0,0,0,1.308-.862,8.078,8.078,0,0,0,1.221-2,5.018,5.018,0,0,0,.494-1.929,1.707,1.707,0,0,0-.281-.872,1.567,1.567,0,0,1-.28-.7.89.89,0,0,1,.232-.611.722.722,0,0,1,.562-.262,1.166,1.166,0,0,1,.62.155,2.346,2.346,0,0,1,.271,1.124,6.96,6.9