4da-a8bd-4720-be8b-988ab060ec4f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f5c7f9d9-7509-4485-89f2-a773efb32e9a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["9ff714da-a8bd-4720-be8b-988ab060ec4f"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is similar to parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R upper S\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math>. When two parallelograms are similar, if the scale factor between their corresponding side lengths is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, the scale factor between their areas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k squared\"><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the length of each side of parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R upper S\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> times the length of its corresponding side of parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math>, so the scale factor between their corresponding side lengths is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math>. It follows that the scale factor between their areas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 squared\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the area, in square centimeters, of parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn></math>. It follows that the area, in square centimeters, of parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R upper S\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis\"><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017718,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"6708546e","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1755117017718,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"518073a0-4d7c-48ab-af96-3d1d19b33661","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"712d1585-79db-452d-ac9b-57931f5f2ae5","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Parallelogram <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to parallelogram <math alttext=\"upper P upper Q upper R upper S\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>P</mi>\n\t<mi>Q</mi>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. The length of each side of parallelogram <math alttext=\"upp