$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><img src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_000_070faa26.png" alt="The figure presents right triangle R S T such that side R T is horizontal, vertex T is to the right of vertex R, and vertex S is above R T. Side R S is labeled 12. Side S T is labeled 5. Angle S is a right angle" width="118" height="54">
        <p class="stem_paragraph ">In triangle <span class="italic">RST</span> above, point <span class="italic">W</span> (not shown)<span class="formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both "></span> lies on <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_001_030e1788.png" alt="line segment R T"></span></span>. What is the value of <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_002_3ce61ff7.png" alt="cosine of angle R S W, minus sine of angle W S T"></span></span> ?</p></p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["0"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 0. Note that no matter where point <span class="italic">W </span>is on <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_003_030e1788.png" alt="side R T"></span>, the sum of the measures of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_004_0fc4c3da.png" alt="angle R S W"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_005_40d438d5.png" alt="angle W S T"></span> is equal to the measure of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_006_df0d98e6.png" alt="angle R S T"></span>, which is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_007_40b6f03d.png" alt="90 degrees"></span>. Thus, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_008_0fc4c3da.png" alt="angle R S W"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_009_40d438d5.png" alt="angle W S T"></span> are complementary angles. Since the cosine of an angle is equal to the sine of its complementary angle, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_010_5541bc48.png" alt="the cosine of angle R S W, equals, the sine of angle W S T"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_011_2a3fb220.png" alt="the cosine of angle R S W, minus, the sine of angle W S T, equals 0"></span>.</p>
$SATQ$, true, 12, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"6933b3d9","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"05777-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \"></div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p><img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_000_070faa26.png\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle R S T such that side R T is horizontal, vertex T is to the right of vertex R, and vertex S is above R T. Side R S is labeled 12. Side S T is labeled 5. Angle S is a right angle\" width=\"118\" height=\"54\">\n        <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In triangle <span class=\"italic\">RST</span> above, point <span class=\"italic\">W</span> (not shown)<span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span> lies on <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_001_030e1788.png\" alt=\"line segment R T\"></span></span>. What is the value of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_002_3ce61ff7.png\" alt=\"cosine of angle R S W, minus sine of angle W S T\"></span></span> ?</p></p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["0"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 0. Note that no matter where point <span class=\"italic\">W </span>is on <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_003_030e1788.png\" alt=\"side R T\"></span>, the sum of the measures of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_004_0fc4c3da.png\" alt=\"angle R S W\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_005_40d438d5.png\" alt=\"angle W S T\"></span> is equal to the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_006_df0d98e6.png\" alt=\"angle R S T\"></span>, which is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_007_40b6f03d.png\" alt=\"90 degrees\"></span>. Thus, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_008_0fc4c3da.png\" alt=\"angle R S W\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_009_40d438d5.png\" alt=\"angle W S T\"></span> are complementary angles. Since the cosine of an angle is equal to the sine of its complementary angle, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_010_5541bc48.png\" alt=\"the cosine of angle R S W, equals, the sine of angle W S T\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6933b3d9/img_011_2a3fb220.png\" alt=\"the cosine of angle R S W, minus, the sine of angle W S T, equals 0\"></span>.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":12,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959630,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"6933b3d9","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1691007959630,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"05777-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"923d2d95-3040-457a-9715-ca51c9a73a8a","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"05777-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \"></div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle R S T such that side R T is horizontal, vertex T is to the right of vertex R, and vertex S is above R T. Side R S is labeled 12. Side S T is labeled 5. Angle S is a right angle\" width=\"118\" height=\"54\">\n        <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In triangle <span class=\"italic\">RST</span> above, point <span class=\"italic\">W</span> (not shown)<span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span> lies on <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment R T\"></span></span>. What is the value of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"cosine of angle R S W, minus sine of angle W S T\"></span></span> ?</p></p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 0. Note that no matter where point <span class=\"italic\">W </span>is on <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"side R T\"></span>, the sum of the measures of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle R S W\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle W S T\"></span> is equal to the measure of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle R S T\"></span>, which is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"90 degrees\"></span>. Thus, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle R S W\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle W S T\"></span> are complementary angles. Since the cosine of an angle is equal to the sine of its complementary angle, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the cosine of angle R S W, equals, the sine of angle W S T\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the cosine of angle R S W, minus, the sine of angle W S T, equals 0\"></span>.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959630,"updateDate":1691007959630,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959630, 1691007959630),
