ct/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_015_1725b68a.png\" alt=\"60 degrees\"></span> from both sides of this equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_016_98c6af41.png\" alt=\"x degrees equals 120 degrees\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_017_a4dd307d.png\" alt=\"the fraction 2 pi over 3\"></span> radians. Therefore, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">AOB, </span>and thus the measure of arc <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_018_2f3bb937.png\" alt=\"A, B\"></span>, is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_019_a4dd307d.png\" alt=\"the fraction 2 pi over 3 \"></span> radians. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_020_4deeec7c.png\" alt=\"the line segment O C \"></span> is a radius of the given circle and its length is 18, the length of the radius of the circle is 18. Therefore, the length of arc <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_021_2f3bb937.png\" alt=\"A, B\"></span> can be calculated as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/69b0d79d/img_022_71c