only */\n            .Rrrrr { font: italic 40px serif; fill: red; }\n        </style>\n    </g>\n</g>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for right triangle\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>One angle is a right angle.</li>\n<li>The measures of the other 2 angles are as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>a°</li>\n<li>13°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the right triangle shown, what is the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"34d9fd45-b377-42fe-844e-653792d32e03","content":"<p><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"60be82e7-9824-43a6-b710-fa0f0fd7a452","content":"<p><math alttext=\"77\"><mn>77</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"421c8fcb-72e1-4bb0-9dfa-1a089435724b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b982b6fb-ace8-41c9-9918-efa8fd19aa74","content":"<p><math alttext=\"103\"><mn>103</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["60be82e7-9824-43a6-b710-fa0f0fd7a452"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The triangle shown is a right triangle, where the interior angle shown with a right angle symbol has a measure of <math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It's shown that the other two interior angles measure <math alttext=\"13 degree\"><mn>13</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"a degree\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>; therefore, <math alttext=\"90 plus 13 plus a equals 180\"><mn>90</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"103 plus a equals 180\"><mn>103</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"103\"><mn>103</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"a equals 77\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>77</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of the other acute interior angle of the right triangle, not the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of the right angle of the right triangle, not the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures, in degrees, of the other two interior angles of the right triangle, not the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357407,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"69f4bbdc","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1730147357407,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"d14a2fdd-4d09-4911-b363-67cb2fe299e3","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"69c9eb07-9e9a-46ce-93fe-b0c6c70d02d4","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"34d9fd45-b377-42fe-844e-653792d32e03"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"77\"><mn>77</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"60be82e7-9824-43a6-b710-fa0f0fd7a452"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"421c8fcb-72e1-4bb0-9dfa-1a089435724b"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"103\"><mn>103</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"b982b6fb-ace8-41c9-9918-efa8fd19aa74"}],"externalid":"d14a2fdd-4d09-4911-b363-67cb2fe299e3","keys":["60be82e7-9824-43a6-b710-fa0f0fd7a452"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The triangle shown is a right triangle, where the interior angle shown with a right angle symbol has a measure of <math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It's shown that the other two interior angles measure <math alttext=\"13 degree\"><mn>13</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"a degree\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>; therefore, <math alttext=\"90 plus 13 plus a equals 180\"><mn>90</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"103 plus a equals 180\"><mn>103</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"103\"><mn>103</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"a equals 77\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>a</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>77</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of the other acute interior angle of the right triangle, not the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the measure, in degrees, of the right angle of the right triangle, not the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures, in degrees, of the other two interior angles of the right triangle, not the value of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"250.0pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 250.0 210.0\" height=\"210.0pt\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A right triangle. Refer to long description.\">\n  <g>\n    <g><defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id